## 2. 🏗️ Architecture & Flow

```
CLIENT (Browser / Mobile App / Postman)
        │
        │  HTTP Request (GET / POST / PUT / DELETE)
        ▼
FLASK REST API  (Your Backend — Python)
        │
        ├── /api/auth       → Authentication (Register, Login)
        ├── /api/products   → Product Catalog (Search, Filter, Reviews)
        ├── /api/cart       → Shopping Cart (Add, Update, Remove)
        ├── /api/orders     → Order Management (Place, Track, Status)
        └── /api/admin      → Admin Dashboard (Stats, Analytics)
        │
        │  SQLAlchemy ORM (Python talks to Database)
        ▼
SQLite DATABASE (app.db)
        │
        ├── users table
        ├── products table
        ├── cart table
        ├── orders table
        ├── order_items table
        └── reviews table
```

**Request Flow Example (User buys a product):**
1. User sends `POST /api/auth/login` → gets a **JWT token**
2. User sends `POST /api/cart/add` with token → item saved in **cart table**
3. User sends `POST /api/orders/` with token → system checks stock, deducts inventory, creates order
4. Admin sends `PUT /api/orders/5/status` → updates order to `shipped`

