## 4. 🗄️ Database Design & Relationships

### Tables & Relationships:
```
users (1) ──────────── (many) orders
users (1) ──────────── (many) cart
users (1) ──────────── (many) reviews
products (1) ─────────── (many) cart
products (1) ─────────── (many) order_items
products (1) ─────────── (many) reviews
orders (1) ──────────── (many) order_items
```

### Key Design Decisions:
| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| Separate `order_items` table | One order can have multiple products |
| `price_at_purchase` in order_items | Product price may change later, order must remember what was paid |
| `status` + `payment_status` both on Order | Payment and fulfillment are separate concerns |
| `role` column on User | Single table handles both users and admins |

