## 10. 🔥 Follow-Up Questions Interviewers May Ask

| They ask... | Strong answer hint |
|---|---|
| "What's a JWT and where is it stored on the client?" | JWT sent in response, client stores in localStorage or cookie, sends as `Authorization: Bearer` header |
| "What's the difference between SQL and NoSQL?" | SQL = structured tables, JOINs, ACID; NoSQL = flexible schema, horizontal scale; you chose SQL because data is relational |
| "What is ORM? Why not write raw SQL?" | ORM maps Python classes to tables; prevents SQL injection; easier to switch databases; trade-off is less control |
| "How do you prevent SQL injection?" | SQLAlchemy ORM uses parameterized queries automatically — no string concatenation in SQL |
| "What does `@wraps(f)` do in your decorator?" | Preserves the original function's name and docstring — without it, all decorated functions would appear as `decorated` in logs |
| "What is CORS and does your API need it?" | Cross-Origin Resource Sharing — if a browser frontend on a different domain calls your API, you need Flask-CORS. You'd add it for production |
| "How would you add refresh tokens?" | Store a long-lived refresh token in DB, access token expires in 15 mins, client calls `/auth/refresh` to get new access token |
| "What is the difference between `flush()` and `commit()`?" | `flush()` sends SQL to DB within the transaction (gets ID) but doesn't finalize; `commit()` makes it permanent |
